Privacy Policy — Wakey

Effective: 21 September 2026
App: Wakey (com.yapps.wakey)

Short version

Wakey collects nothing, sends nothing, and has no internet permission. Everything it saves is
stored on your device. There are no accounts, no ads, no analytics and no tracking.

What Wakey stores

On your device only:

Data	Why
Sleep cycle length	Your setting, used in the calculation
Time to fall asleep	Your setting, used in the calculation
Saved wake times (up to 8)	The favourites shown on the home screen

That is the complete list. Wakey does not store your alarms, your sleep, your location, your
contacts, your device identifiers, or anything about how you use the app.

What Wakey does not do
No internet permission is declared, so the app cannot send data anywhere.
No analytics, crash reporting, advertising or tracking SDKs of any kind.
No account, no sign-in, no email address required.
No data is sold, shared or disclosed to anyone, because none is collected.
Permissions

Wakey declares one permission:

com.android.alarm.permission.SET_ALARM — lets Wakey open your Clock app with a time
already filled in when you tap a result. You always confirm the alarm in your own Clock app;
Wakey never creates one silently, and it cannot read alarms you already have.
Other apps and links
Your Clock app. Tapping a result opens your phone's Clock app with a time and a label.
What that app does with it is covered by its own privacy policy, not this one.
The "Why 90 minutes?" link in Settings opens a page on sleephealthfoundation.org.au
in your browser. Your browser and that website apply their own policies from that point on.

Wakey has no control over, and takes no responsibility for, either.

Children

Wakey is not directed at children. It collects no personal data from anyone, of any age.

Deleting your data

Uninstall the app, or use Settings → Apps → Wakey → Storage → Clear data. Both remove
everything Wakey has saved.

Changes

If this policy changes, the effective date above changes with it, and the updated version is
published at the same address.

